design_implications:
q-values in poker terms. Abstract actions: FOLD, CHECK/CALL, BET f·pot for f in {~0.33, 0.5, 0.75, 1, 1.5}, preflop opens {2-2.5, 3 BB}, ALL-IN. Map to CodinGame 'BET amount' (chips added, at least the listed BET_min).
For each a, and k = 1..K using common random numbers across actions:
- draw y^(k) ~ b(·|I) and a deck permutation ω^(k);
- play a, then continue to the end of the hand: us with π_θ, opponent j with σ_j(·|y_j^(k), s), cards from ω^(k);
- G_k(a) = U(terminal).
Then q̂(a) = mean_k G_k(a). When everyone left is all-in, or at a river showdown, replace the sampled runout with the exact expectation over remaining boards (≤990 turn+river runouts, or a preflop table). A single call on the river needs no rollout: q(call) = Σ_y b(y)·U(win/tie/lose).

components.description:
OMPEval-style rank keys with a perfect hash built at start-up (scratchpad/poker_research/evals/pe7c.hpp). It has been verified against a full 133.8M-hand enumeration and against OMPEval and PHEvaluator. It needs no payload.

Uses:
- showdowns in rollouts;
- exact runout enumeration at all-in leaves (flop to river: 990 two-card runouts x 2-4 evaluations, ~10-20 us);
- per-combo hand-strength features.

~148 inputs, split into a public part p(s) (~100) and a private part x(y) (~48), so that the first layer factorises for fast range updates.

Public part p(s):
- N alive and N in hand (one-hot);
- street;
- position relative to the dealer, SB and BB, and players left to act;
- per seat: log(1+stack/BB), stack share, chips committed this hand/pot, in-hand and all-in flags;
- log pot/BB, toCall/pot, toCall/stack, log SPR, minRaise/pot;
- raises this street, last aggressor, per-street summary (raises, max bet/pot, whether I raised);
- log2 BB level, hands to the next level, round/600;
- W(stacks) payout vector and my slope s*BB (tournament pressure);
- board texture (paired, trips, monotone/two-tone, straight possible, top rank, connectedness).
The opponent's exact continuous bet size enters here as bet/pot and bet/stack, so off-tree sizes need no translation inside the net.

Private part x(y):
- rank1/rank2/suited one-hot (27);
- preflop equity vs a random hand (169-entry table);
- made-hand category (9) and its rank percentile among the 1,326 combos on this board;
- EHS and EHS^2 by 32-64-sample Monte Carlo;
- flush and straight draw, overcards, both-cards-used, nut-flush blocker.

The private part is computed for all live combos once per street (<=1 ms) and cached.

Architecture: MLP 148 -> 256 -> 128 -> 64 -> [8 policy logits + 4 place logits], ReLU (or clipped ReLU for integer inference). About 80k parameters (37.9k + 32.9k + 8.3k + 0.8k).

Abstract actions:
- FOLD (masked when checking is free);
- CHECK/CALL;
- MIN (the offered BET_min);
- raises of 0.33, 0.66, 1.0 and 2.0 pot;
- ALL-IN.
A raise to f*pot means raiseTo = currentBet + f*(pot + toCall). Duplicates are masked: a size that collapses to MIN, or that reaches the stack and so becomes ALL-IN.

Preflop at 4 players this gives opens of 2 / 2.5 (0.33 pot) / 3 / 4 / 7 BB. That covers the 2-6 BB opens the field uses.

The place head (P(finish place | my infostate)) is the Ataraxos-style value head. It is used only as a leaf when a rollout hits its depth cap, and as a control variate.

Inference:
- AVX2 fp32 or int16, with #pragma GCC optimize("O3") before the includes and always_inline, as in crossfish.
- The first layer is split, h1 = relu(A*p + B*x(y) + b), so A*p is computed once per public state and each combo costs only B*x(y) plus the upper layers (~53k MACs).

Reuse the crossfish pipeline: cg_minify.py, the CJK14 packer at 14 bits per counted UTF-16 character (minification.md:249-275), and per-row quantisation, with GPTQ-style rounding calibrated on self-play decisions.

Budget:
- code: ~28k chars (engine 5k, evaluator 2.7k, parser/state 4k, features 3k, MLP 2k, beliefs 1.5k, search 3k, W/ICM 1.5k, decoder 1k, timing and misc 4k);
- payload: policy 46k + W 3k, plus the optional equity table at 8.1k;
- total: ~78-86k chars, leaving 14-22k margin, which could buy ~25-40k more int8 params or 6-bit coding.

The C++ engine plus a match runner that uses duplicate seeds with every seat rotation (2, 6 or 24 permutations for N = 2, 3, 4), scored by the TrueSkill-implied payout and by pairwise 'finished ahead' rates.

Baselines:
- the calling-station boss;
- the gpoussel MC-equity-vs-pot-odds clone;
- a Tuo-style pure push/fold bot;
- a kovi-like nit with rules;
- a Waffle3z-like LAG (raises 90% of unopened pots at 2-6 BB and c-bets 97%);
- maniacs (open to 25-100 BB and call 100% of all-ins);
- behaviour-cloned nets from reconstructed public replays (reconstruct.py: 22.9k decisions from 120 games, extendable).

This replaces what the Ataraxos paper did with human and prior-bot evaluations.

first_steps:
Build the local arena:
- fast in-process mode;
- duplicate seeds with seat rotation;
- 41/34/25% table mix (4p/3p/HU);
- archetype zoo: gpoussel port, Tuo push/fold, kovi-style nit, Waffle3z-style LAG, BrandV-style jammer, maniac, calling station, the boss;
- SPRT through crossfish tools/sprt_merge.py.
Primary metric: pairwise finish-ahead rate p.
